  "appChannelGuideEntry": "First time? Tap the \"?\" at the top-right of a card to see how to get each parameter",
  "appChannelGuideOpen": "Setup steps",
  "appChannelGuideTitleWecom": "WeCom Self-built App · Setup Steps",
  "appChannelGuideTitleFeishu": "Feishu Self-built App · Setup Steps",
  "appChannelGuidePrepWecom": "Prerequisite: WeCom admin (or app admin) access, and a self-built app created in the admin console.",
  "appChannelGuidePrepFeishu": "Prerequisite: Feishu Open Platform developer access. Publishing a version requires admin approval.",
  "appChannelGuideWecomS1": "Get the Corp ID (corpid)",
  "appChannelGuideWecomS1Desc": "Admin console (work.weixin.qq.com) → \"My Enterprise\" → \"Enterprise Info\" → scroll to the bottom and copy the Enterprise ID.",
  "appChannelGuideWecomS2": "Create a self-built app",
  "appChannelGuideWecomS2Desc": "\"App Management\" → \"Apps\" → \"Self-built\" → \"Create App\"; fill in the name and icon.",
  "appChannelGuideWecomS3": "Get AgentId and Secret",
  "appChannelGuideWecomS3Desc": "Open the app you just created: the AgentId (digits only) is shown at the top; click \"View\" next to Secret, send the prompt to WeCom, then copy the secret (this is the corpsecret / Secret field in this app).",
  "appChannelGuideWecomS4": "Set visible range (recipients)",
  "appChannelGuideWecomS4Desc": "App details → \"Visible Range\": add the members/departments that should receive pushes. Leave the Recipient field empty to push to all visible members (@all); multiple user IDs can be separated by |.",
  "appChannelGuideWecomS5": "(Optional) Configure trusted IP",
  "appChannelGuideWecomS5Desc": "If the enterprise enforces \"Trusted IP\": app details → \"Developer Interface\" → \"Trusted IP\" and add the phone's egress IP; otherwise skip.",
  "appChannelGuideWecomS6": "Fill in and test",
  "appChannelGuideWecomS6Desc": "Enter the Corp ID / AgentId / Secret, tap the card's \"Test\" button to confirm delivery, then save.",
  "appChannelGuideFeishuS1": "Create an enterprise self-built app",
  "appChannelGuideFeishuS1Desc": "Open the Feishu Developer Console (open.feishu.cn) → \"Create Enterprise Self-built App\"; fill in name, description and icon.",
  "appChannelGuideFeishuS2": "Get App ID and App Secret",
  "appChannelGuideFeishuS2Desc": "App details → \"Credentials & Basic Info\" → copy the App ID and App Secret.",
  "appChannelGuideFeishuS3": "Enable message permissions",
  "appChannelGuideFeishuS3Desc": "In \"Permissions\", search for and enable im:message (send single chat messages) and im:message:send_as_bot (send as the app).",
  "appChannelGuideFeishuS4": "Create a version and publish",
  "appChannelGuideFeishuS4Desc": "\"Version Management & Release\" → \"Create Version\" → request release. Permissions take effect only after admin approval (pushes fail before that).",
  "appChannelGuideFeishuS5": "Get the recipient ID",
  "appChannelGuideFeishuS5Desc": "Set receive_id_type to chat_id (group) or open_id (user). Use the API Explorer with im/v1/chats to get a chat_id; open_id can be found in contact details or via the explorer.",
  "appChannelGuideFeishuS6": "Fill in and test",
  "appChannelGuideFeishuS6Desc": "Enter App ID / App Secret / recipient type / recipient ID, tap the card's \"Test\" button to confirm delivery, then save.",
  "appChannelGuideNoteTitle": "Notes",
  "appChannelGuideNote1": "The secret is usually only visible at creation time — keep it safe; it is stored encrypted in this app.",
  "appChannelGuideNote2": "Self-hosted deployment: replace the API base URL with your own (leave empty to use the official one).",
  "appChannelGuideNote3": "Common causes of push failure: permissions not granted / app version not published / recipient not in the visible range / wrong Secret or recipient ID.",
  "appChannelGuideNote4": "App channels and Webhook channels are independent and can be enabled together; delivery results and retries behave the same as Webhook channels.",
  "appChannelGuideClose": "Got it",
  "appChannelGuideNote5": "A custom API base URL must use HTTPS (plain http is rejected by the system); self-signed certificates are not trusted and will fail to connect — use a proper certificate, or leave it empty to use the official endpoint.",
